# Deny-by-default allowlist. `make dsco` only needs src/, include/, vendor/,
# the Makefile, and the specific bootstrap/bake-data scripts it shells out to
# (Makefile:606-608: `bash scripts/bake_data.sh data src/generated include`,
# which globs `find data -maxdepth 1 -type f`). Everything else in this
# monorepo — reports/, environments/, email-mcp/, research_notes/, generated/,
# 640MB+ of data/ subdirectories, etc. — is irrelevant to the build and would
# otherwise balloon the context to multiple GB.
#
# This is also a deliberate security boundary, not just a size one:
# data/dsco_secrets.txt sits directly under data/ (matching the Makefile's
# bake-data glob) and is real local, gitignored credential material — if it
# were ever swept into a build context, `bake_data.sh` would compile its
# contents directly into the `dsco` binary as a linked-in byte array,
# extractable from the image with `strings`. It is intentionally NOT in the
# allowlist below, and never should be.
**

!Makefile
!scripts/bootstrap.sh
!scripts/bake_data.sh
!scripts/bake_data.py
!scripts/embed_lingo.py
!src/**
!include/**
!vendor/**
!lingo/**
!gsl/**
!docker/entrypoint.sh

# Exact files only — no directory-level `data/` rule, so nothing new dropped
# into data/ is ever included without an explicit decision to add it here.
!data/abliteration_docs_index.json
!data/constants_env_index.json
!data/tool_embeddings.bin
